From 81226b4f17dd6bd05bbff91fffba4615263137ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam <sam@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:43:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cli): remove web access and add fullscreen terminal

- Remove SearchWeb/FetchUrlContent tools plus the web, url, google and http
  context providers, their prompts, permissions, docs and tests.
- Disable direct network clients in terminal-security, including curl, wget,
  ssh, scp, Invoke-WebRequest, Start-BitsTransfer and Test-NetConnection, while
  leaving internal LLM/auth networking untouched.
- Add an alternate-screen CLI transcript with an internal virtual viewport,
  measured row heights, PageUp/PageDown, Home/End, shift+arrow and mouse wheel
  scrolling, plus automatic redraw on resize.
- Keep the input box pinned at the bottom, ignore mouse escape sequences in the
  prompt, and restore the terminal on unmount or exit.
- Add --no-fullscreen and CONTINUE_CLI_NO_FULLSCREEN for classic scrollback.
